AffineVariety ** AffineVariety -- Cartesian product of two affine varieties
***************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note **: (Macaulay2Doc)_st_st,

Description
===========

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        X ** Y
  * Inputs:
      * X, an *note affine variety: AffineVariety,, 
      * Y, an *note affine variety: AffineVariety,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note affine variety: AffineVariety,, the Cartesian product $X
        \times Y$
+-----------------------------+
|i1 : X = Spec QQ[x,y]        |
|                             |
|o1 = X                       |
|                             |
|o1 : AffineVariety           |
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : Y = X ** X              |
|                             |
|o2 = Y                       |
|                             |
|o2 : AffineVariety           |
+-----------------------------+
|i3 : describe Y              |
|                             |
|o3 = Spec(QQ[x , y , x , y ])|
|              0   0   1   1  |
+-----------------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        X ** R
  * Inputs:
      * X, an *note affine variety: AffineVariety,, 
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note affine variety: AffineVariety,, the Cartesian product $X
        \times \mathrm{Spec} R$
+----------------------+
|i4 : Z = X ** QQ[t]   |
|                      |
|o4 = Z                |
|                      |
|o4 : AffineVariety    |
+----------------------+
|i5 : describe Z       |
|                      |
|o5 = Spec(QQ[x..y, t])|
+----------------------+

Caveat
======

Cartesian products of non-affine varieties are not yet implemented in this
package, but see *note cartesianProduct(NormalToricVariety):
(NormalToricVarieties)cartesianProduct_lpSequence_rp, for another
implementation.

