codim(CoherentSheaf) -- codimension of the support of a coherent sheaf on a projective variety
**********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note codim: (Macaulay2Doc)codim,
  * Usage: 
        codim F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note coherent sheaf: CoherentSheaf,, a coherent sheaf over a
        *note ProjectiveVariety: ProjectiveVariety, X
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Generic => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,

Description
===========

Computes the codimension of the support of F as given by dim(R) - dim(M) where
M is the module representing F over the homogeneous coordinate ring R of X.
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/31991[a,b,c,d];                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialCurveIdeal(R,{1,3,5})                    |
|                                                          |
|             2         2     2    3    2                  |
|o2 = ideal (c  - b*d, b c - a d, b  - a c)                |
|                                                          |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : projplane = Proj(R)                                  |
|                                                          |
|o3 = projplane                                            |
|                                                          |
|o3 : ProjectiveVariety                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : II = sheaf module I                                  |
|                                                          |
|o4 = image | c2-bd b2c-a2d b3-a2c |                       |
|                                                          |
|                                                         1|
|o4 : coherent sheaf on projplane, subsheaf of OO          |
|                                                projplane |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : can = sheafExt^1(II,OO_projplane^1(-4))              |
|                                                          |
|o5 = cokernel | a2 -b c |                                 |
|              | b2 -c d |                                 |
|                                                          |
|                                                         2|
|o5 : coherent sheaf on projplane, quotient of OO          |
|                                                projplane |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : codim can                                            |
|                                                          |
|o6 = 2                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The returned value is the usual codimension if R is an integral domain or, more
generally, equidimensional.

See also
========

  * *note dim(Module): (Macaulay2Doc)dim_lpModule_rp, -- compute the Krull
    dimension

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note codim(CoherentSheaf): codim_lpCoherentSheaf_rp, -- codimension of the
    support of a coherent sheaf on a projective variety
