coherent sheaves
****************

The main reason to implement algebraic varieties is support the computation of
sheaf cohomology of coherent sheaves, which doesn't have an immediate
description in terms of graded modules.


In this example, we use *note cotangentSheaf: cotangentSheaf, to produce the
cotangent sheaf on a K3 surface and compute its sheaf cohomology.
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d]/(a^4+b^4+c^4+d^4);        |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = Proj R                                |
|                                               |
|o2 = X                                         |
|                                               |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Omega = cotangentSheaf X                  |
|                                               |
|o3 = cokernel {2} | c  0  0  d  0   a3  b3 0  ||
|              {2} | a  d  0  0  b3  -c3 0  0  ||
|              {2} | -b 0  d  0  a3  0   c3 0  ||
|              {2} | 0  b  a  0  -d3 0   0  c3 ||
|              {2} | 0  -c 0  a  0   -d3 0  b3 ||
|              {2} | 0  0  -c -b 0   0   d3 a3 ||
|                                               |
|                                         6     |
|o3 : coherent sheaf on X, quotient of OO  (-2) |
|                                        X      |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : HH^1(Omega)                               |
|                                               |
|       20                                      |
|o4 = QQ                                        |
|                                               |
|o4 : QQ-module, free                           |
+-----------------------------------------------+
Use the function *note sheaf: sheaf, to convert a graded module to a coherent
sheaf, and *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)module, to get the graded module back
again.
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : F = sheaf coker matrix {{a,b}}       |
|                                          |
|o5 = cokernel | a b |                     |
|                                          |
|                                         1|
|o5 : coherent sheaf on X, quotient of OO  |
|                                        X |
+------------------------------------------+
|i6 : module F                             |
|                                          |
|o6 = cokernel | a b |                     |
|                                          |
|                            1             |
|o6 : R-module, quotient of R              |
+------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note HH^ZZ CoherentSheaf: HH^ZZ_lpProjectiveVariety_cmCoherentSheaf_rp, --
    cohomology of a coherent sheaf on a projective variety
  * *note HH^ZZ SumOfTwists: HH^ZZ SumOfTwists, -- coherent sheaf cohomology
    module
