cotangentSheaf -- cotangent sheaf of a projective variety
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        cotangentSheaf X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note projective variety: ProjectiveVariety,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * MinimalGenerators => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value true, whether to *note prune: (Macaulay2Doc)prune, the
        result before returning it
      * Strategy => ..., default value null
  * Outputs:
      * a *note coherent sheaf: CoherentSheaf,, 

Description
===========

This method computes the cotangent sheaf of the projective variety $X$. The
method used is to take the middle homology of the sequence associated to the
Jacobian: --finish

As an example we verify the Gauss-Bonnet theorem on a plane quartic curve:

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = Proj QQ[x,y,z]/(x^4+y^4+z^4)   |
|                                        |
|o1 = X                                  |
|                                        |
|o1 : ProjectiveVariety                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : genus X                            |
|                                        |
|o2 = 3                                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : omega = cotangentSheaf X           |
|                                        |
|        1                               |
|o3 = OO  (1)                            |
|       X                                |
|                                        |
|o3 : coherent sheaf on X, free of rank 1|
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : degree omega                       |
|                                        |
|o4 = 4                                  |
+----------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note idealSheaf: idealSheaf, -- ideal sheaf of a projective variety
  * *note tangentSheaf: tangentSheaf, -- tangent sheaf of a projective variety
  * *note ProjectiveVariety: ProjectiveVariety, -- the class of all projective
    varieties

