degree(ProjectiveVariety)
*************************

  * Function: *note degree: (Macaulay2Doc)degree,
  * Usage: 
        degree X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note projective variety: ProjectiveVariety,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the degree of X

Description
===========

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/32003[x,y,z];             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^4-4*x*y*z^2-z^4-y^4);|
|                                      |
|o2 : Ideal of S                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : R = S/I;                         |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : X = variety I                    |
|                                      |
|o4 = X                                |
|                                      |
|o4 : ProjectiveVariety                |
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : degree X                         |
|                                      |
|o5 = 4                                |
+--------------------------------------+
The degree of a projective variety X = V(I) = Proj R is the degree of the
homogeneous coordinate ring R = S/I of X.
+-------------------------+
|i6 : degree X == degree I|
|                         |
|o6 = true                |
+-------------------------+
|i7 : degree X == degree R|
|                         |
|o7 = true                |
+-------------------------+

