dim(AffineVariety) -- dimension of the affine variety
*****************************************************

  * Function: *note dim: (Macaulay2Doc)dim,
  * Usage: 
        dim V
  * Inputs:
      * V, an *note affine variety: AffineVariety,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,

Description
===========

Computes the dimension of the affine algebraic set V as the Krull dimension of
its affine coordinate ring.
+------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y];               |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : point = ideal(x,y);            |
|                                    |
|o2 : Ideal of R                     |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : line = ideal(2*x+3*y-1);       |
|                                    |
|o3 : Ideal of R                     |
+------------------------------------+
|i4 : V=Spec(R/intersect(point,line))|
|                                    |
|o4 = V                              |
|                                    |
|o4 : AffineVariety                  |
+------------------------------------+
|i5 : dim V                          |
|                                    |
|o5 = 1                              |
+------------------------------------+
|i6 : Z=Spec(R/(point+line))         |
|                                    |
|o6 = Z                              |
|                                    |
|o6 : AffineVariety                  |
+------------------------------------+
|i7 : dim Z                          |
|                                    |
|o7 = -1                             |
+------------------------------------+

See also
