euler(ProjectiveVariety) -- topological Euler characteristic of a (smooth) projective variety
*********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note euler: (Macaulay2Doc)euler,
  * Usage: 
        euler V
  * Inputs:
      * V, a *note projective variety: ProjectiveVariety,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the topological Euler
        characteristics of the variety V

Description
===========

The command computes the topological Euler characteristic of the (smooth)
projective variety V as an alternated sum of its Hodge numbers. The Hodge
numbers can be computed directly using the command *note hh: hh,.


A smooth plane quartic curve has genus 3 and topological Euler characteristic
-4:
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Quartic = Proj(QQ[x_0..x_2]/ideal(x_0^4+x_1^4+x_2^4))|
|                                                          |
|o1 = Quartic                                              |
|                                                          |
|o1 : ProjectiveVariety                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : euler(Quartic)                                       |
|                                                          |
|o2 = -4                                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------------+


The topological Euler characteristic of a smooth quintic hypersurface in
projective fourspace is -200:
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Quintic = Proj(QQ[x_0..x_4]/ideal(x_0^5+x_1^5+x_2^5+x_3^5+x_4^5-101*x_0*|
|                                                                             |
|o3 = Quintic                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : ProjectiveVariety                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_1*x_2*x_3*x_4))                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : euler(Quintic)                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = -200                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

No test is made to see if the projective variety is smooth

See also
========

  * *note Proj: Proj, -- make a projective variety
  * *note genus: (Macaulay2Doc)genus,
  * *note hh: hh, -- Hodge numbers of a smooth projective variety

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note euler(ProjectiveVariety): euler_lpProjectiveVariety_rp, --
    topological Euler characteristic of a (smooth) projective variety
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

