hilbertPolynomial(CoherentSheaf) -- compute the Hilbert polynomial of the coherent sheaf
****************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note hilbertPolynomial: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertPolynomial,
  * Usage: 
        hilbertPolynomial S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note coherent sheaf: CoherentSheaf,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Projective: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertPolynomial_lp_pd_pd_pd_
        cmProjective=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value true,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note projective Hilbert polynomial:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial,, unless the option
        Projective is false

Description
===========

We compute the *note Hilbert polynomial: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertPolynomial, of a
coherent sheaf.
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x_0..x_2];                        |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : V = Proj R;                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = sheaf(image matrix {{x_0^3+x_1^3+x_2^3}})|
|                                                  |
|o3 = image | x_0^3+x_1^3+x_2^3 |                  |
|                                                  |
|                                         1        |
|o3 : coherent sheaf on V, subsheaf of OO          |
|                                        V         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : h = hilbertPolynomial S                      |
|                                                  |
|o4 = 3*P  - 3*P  + P                              |
|        0      1    2                             |
|                                                  |
|o4 : ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial                  |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : hilbertPolynomial(S, Projective=>false)      |
|                                                  |
|     1 2   3                                      |
|o5 = -i  - -i + 1                                 |
|     2     2                                      |
|                                                  |
|o5 : QQ[i]                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------+

