Hom(CoherentSheaf,CoherentSheaf) -- global Hom
**********************************************

  * Function: *note Hom: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom,
  * Usage: 
        Hom(F, G)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note sheaf of rings: SheafOfRings, or a *note coherent sheaf:
        CoherentSheaf,,
      * G, a *note sheaf of rings: SheafOfRings, or a *note coherent sheaf:
        CoherentSheaf,,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note DegreeLimit: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom, => ..., default value null, 
      * *note MinimalGenerators: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom, => ..., default value true,
      * *note Strategy: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom, => ..., default value null, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, representing a vector space over
        the coefficient field of $X$

Description
===========

If F or G is a *note sheaf of rings: SheafOfRings,, it is regarded as a sheaf
of modules in the evident way.

Both F and G must be coherent sheaves on the same projective variety or scheme
$X$.

The result is the sheaf associated to the graded module Hom(module F, module
G).

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                                     |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P3 = Proj R                                       |
|                                                       |
|o2 = P3                                                |
|                                                       |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = monomialCurveIdeal(R, {1,3,4})                |
|                                                       |
|                        3      2     2    2    3    2  |
|o3 = ideal (b*c - a*d, c  - b*d , a*c  - b d, b  - a c)|
|                                                       |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : G = sheaf module I                                |
|                                                       |
|o4 = image | bc-ad c3-bd2 ac2-b2d b3-a2c |             |
|                                                       |
|                                           1           |
|o4 : coherent sheaf on P3, subsheaf of OO              |
|                                         P3            |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Hom(OO_P3, G(3))                                  |
|                                                       |
|       7                                               |
|o5 = QQ                                                |
|                                                       |
|o5 : QQ-module, free                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : HH^0(G(3))                                        |
|                                                       |
|       7                                               |
|o6 = QQ                                                |
|                                                       |
|o6 : QQ-module, free                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

