ideal(Variety) -- returns the defining ideal
********************************************

  * Function: *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)ideal,
  * Usage: 
        ideal X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note variety: Variety,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, which is the defining ideal of X

Description
===========

A *note variety: Variety, is defined by a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,.
This function returns the defining ideal of the ring of X.
+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[w,x,y,z];                       |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = Spec(R/(y^2-x*z,x^2*y-z^2,x^3-y*z))|
|                                            |
|o2 = X                                      |
|                                            |
|o2 : AffineVariety                          |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : ideal X                                |
|                                            |
|             2         2     2   3          |
|o3 = ideal (y  - x*z, x y - z , x  - y*z)   |
|                                            |
|o3 : Ideal of R                             |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : ring X                                 |
|                                            |
|                    R                       |
|o4 = ------------------------------         |
|       2         2     2   3                |
|     (y  - x*z, x y - z , x  - y*z)         |
|                                            |
|o4 : QuotientRing                           |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Y = Proj(R/(x^2-w*y, x*y-w*z, x*z-y^2))|
|                                            |
|o5 = Y                                      |
|                                            |
