sheafExt -- sheaf extension of coherent sheaves
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        sheafExt^n(F,G)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * F, a *note sheaf of rings: SheafOfRings, or a *note coherent sheaf:
        CoherentSheaf,,
      * G, a *note sheaf of rings: SheafOfRings, or a *note coherent sheaf:
        CoherentSheaf,,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note coherent sheaf: CoherentSheaf,, the n-th sheaf extension of F
        and G

Description
===========

If F or G is a *note sheaf of rings: SheafOfRings,, it is regarded as a sheaf
of modules in the evident way.

Both F and S must be coherent sheaves on the same projective variety or scheme
$X$.

The result is the sheaf associated to the graded module Ext^n(module F, module
G).

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = Proj QQ[x,y]                   |
|                                        |
|o1 = X                                  |
|                                        |
|o1 : ProjectiveVariety                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : sheafExt^1(OO_X^1(2), OO_X^1(-11)) |
|                                        |
|o2 = 0                                  |
|                                        |
|o2 : coherent sheaf on X, free of rank 0|
+----------------------------------------+

