SheafMap ^** ZZ -- repeatedly tensors a map
*******************************************

  * Operator: *note ^**: (Macaulay2Doc)^_st_st,
  * Usage: 
        f ^** n
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note morphism of sheaves: SheafMap,, a sheaf map
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a non-negative integer
  * Outputs:
      * a *note morphism of sheaves: SheafMap,, the sheaf map f tensor n times

Description
===========

This will create a sheaf map g which is the tensor of f with itself.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                      |
|                                        |
|o1 = R                                  |
|                                        |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                     |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = variety R                      |
|                                        |
|o2 = X                                  |
|                                        |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = sheafHom(OO_X, OO_X)           |
|                                        |
|        1                               |
|o3 = OO                                 |
|       X                                |
|                                        |
|o3 : coherent sheaf on X, free of rank 1|
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : g = f ^** 2                        |
|                                        |
|        1                               |
|o4 = OO                                 |
|       X                                |
|                                        |
|o4 : coherent sheaf on X, free of rank 1|
+----------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note SheafMap ^** ZZ: SheafMap ^_st_st ZZ, -- repeatedly tensors a map
