SheafOfRings ^ List -- make a graded free coherent sheaf
********************************************************

  * Operator: *note ^: (Macaulay2Doc)^,
  * Usage: 
        M = R^{i,j,k,...}
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note sheaf of rings: SheafOfRings,
      * {i,j,k, ...}, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of integers or lists
        of integers
  * Outputs:
      * a *note coherent sheaf: CoherentSheaf,, , a graded free coherent sheaf
        whose generators have degrees -i, -j, -k, ...

Description
===========

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d]/(a*b*c*d)             |
|                                        |
|o1 = R                                  |
|                                        |
|o1 : QuotientRing                       |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = Proj R                         |
|                                        |
|o2 = X                                  |
|                                        |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : OO_X^{-1,-2,3}                     |
|                                        |
|        1           1           1       |
|o3 = OO  (-1) ++ OO  (-2) ++ OO  (3)    |
|       X           X           X        |
|                                        |
|o3 : coherent sheaf on X, free of rank 3|
+----------------------------------------+


If i, j, ... are lists of integers, then they represent multi-degrees, as in
*note graded and multigraded polynomial rings: (Macaulay2Doc)graded and
multigraded polynomial rings,.
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Y = Proj (QQ[x,y,z,Degrees=>{{1,0},{1,-1},{1,-2}}])|
|                                                        |
|o4 = Y                                                  |
|                                                        |
|o4 : ProjectiveVariety                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : OO_Y^{{1,2},{-1,3}}                                |
|                                                        |
|        1              1                                |
|o5 = OO   (1, 2) ++ OO   (-1, 3)                        |
|       Y              Y                                 |
|                                                        |
|o5 : coherent sheaf on Y, free of rank 2                |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : degrees oo                                         |
|                                                        |
|o6 = {{-1, -2}, {1, -3}}                                |
|                                                        |
|o6 : List                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note OO: OO, -- the structure sheaf
  * *note Proj: Proj, -- make a projective variety
  * *note degrees: (Macaulay2Doc)degrees, -- degrees of generators
  * graded and multigraded polynomial rings (missing documentation)

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note SheafOfRings ^ List: SheafOfRings ^ List, -- make a graded free
    coherent sheaf
