varieties
*********

We may use *note Spec: Spec, to create an affine scheme (or algebraic variety)
with a specified coordinate ring and *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)ring, to recover
the ring.
+--------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/2[x,y,z]|
|                    |
|o1 = R              |
|                    |
|o1 : PolynomialRing |
+--------------------+
|i2 : X = Spec R     |
|                    |
|o2 = X              |
|                    |
|o2 : AffineVariety  |
+--------------------+
|i3 : ring X         |
|                    |
|o3 = R              |
|                    |
|o3 : PolynomialRing |
+--------------------+
|i4 : dim X          |
|                    |
|o4 = 3              |
+--------------------+
The variety X is a 3-dimensional affine space.


We may form products.
+-------------------------------------+
|i5 : X ** X                          |
|                                     |
|          ZZ                         |
|o5 = Spec(--[x , y , z , x , y , z ])|
|           2  0   0   0   1   1   1  |
|                                     |
|o5 : AffineVariety                   |
+-------------------------------------+
|i6 : dim oo                          |
|                                     |
|o6 = 6                               |
+-------------------------------------+


We may use *note Proj: Proj, to create a projective scheme (or algebraic
variety) with a specified homogeneous coordinate ring.
+----------------------+
|i7 : Y = Proj R       |
|                      |
|o7 = Y                |
|                      |
|o7 : ProjectiveVariety|
+----------------------+
|i8 : ring Y           |
|                      |
|o8 = R                |
|                      |
|o8 : PolynomialRing   |
+----------------------+
|i9 : dim Y            |
|                      |
|o9 = 2                |
+----------------------+
The most important reason for introducing the notion of algebraic variety into
a computer algebra system is to support the notion of coherent sheaf.  See
*note coherent sheaves: coherent sheaves, for information about that.


For more details about varieties, see *note Variety: Variety,.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Varieties/doc-varieties.m2:48:0.

