variety(Ideal) -- the closed projective subvariety defined by an ideal
**********************************************************************

  * Function: *note variety: variety_lpCoherentSheaf_rp,
  * Usage: 
        variety I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a homogeneous ideal
  * Outputs:
      * a *note variety: Variety,, the closed subvariety defined by an ideal

Description
===========

In the example, we compute the dimension of a line in the projective plane.
+----------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x..z]     |
|                      |
|o1 = R                |
|                      |
|o1 : PolynomialRing   |
+----------------------+
|i2 : variety ideal x  |
|                      |
|          R           |
|o2 = Proj(-)          |
|          x           |
|                      |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety|
+----------------------+
|i3 : dim oo           |
|                      |
|o3 = 1                |
+----------------------+

Caveat
======

An alternative task for this function would be to define the affine subvariety,
so if something like this eventually becomes useful, we may have to redesign
it.  Suggestions welcome.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note variety(Ideal): variety_lpIdeal_rp, -- the closed projective
    subvariety defined by an ideal
