variety(Ring) -- the variety previously associated to a given ring
******************************************************************

  * Function: *note variety: variety_lpCoherentSheaf_rp,
  * Usage: 
        variety S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the intersection ring of a
        variety $X$, say, or the homogeneous (Cox) ring of a normal toric
        variety, or another ring that has been associated to a variety, or an
        element in such a ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note variety: Variety,, $X$, the variety associated with S

Description
===========

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : needsPackage "NormalToricVarieties"|
|                                        |
|o1 = NormalToricVarieties               |
|                                        |
|o1 : Package                            |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = toricProjectiveSpace 1         |
|                                        |
|o2 = X                                  |
|                                        |
|o2 : NormalToricVariety                 |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = ring X                         |
|                                        |
|o3 = S                                  |
|                                        |
|o3 : PolynomialRing                     |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : X === variety S                    |
|                                        |
|o4 = true                               |
+----------------------------------------+
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : needsPackage "Schubert2"                  |
|                                               |
|o5 = Schubert2                                 |
|                                               |
|o5 : Package                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Y = abstractProjectiveSpace 1             |
|                                               |
|o6 = Y                                         |
|                                               |
|o6 : a flag bundle with subquotient ranks {2:1}|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i7 : IY = intersectionRing Y                   |
|                                               |
|o7 = IY                                        |
|                                               |
|o7 : QuotientRing                              |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i8 : Y === variety IY                          |
|                                               |
|o8 = true                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------+

For package developers: All this function does is to look up the symbol variety
in S. This is currently used in two packages, but can be used in other
settings, if desired.

Code
====

../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/Varieties.m2:220:17-220:62: --source code:
variety Ring  := S -> if S.?variety then S.variety else Proj S

See also
========

  * *note NormalToricVarieties: (NormalToricVarieties)Top, -- routines for
    working with normal toric varieties and related objects
  * *note Schubert2: (Schubert2)Top, -- characteristic classes for varieties
    without equations

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note variety(Ring): variety_lpRing_rp, -- the variety previously
    associated to a given ring
